@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- The worked weather-tool executor relies on registry validation, does not fabricate a location when called without one, and preserves schema-valid input including an explicitly selected unit ([validated by: does not fabricate a fallback location outside the registry contract](../../src/orchestration/tools/weather-tool.test.ts#L4); [validated by: preserves schema-valid weather input without changing its units](../../src/orchestration/tools/weather-tool.test.ts#L10)).
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16); [validated by: returns a required-property rejection before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L20)).
+- A missing required property nested inside another object is identified by its complete property path, including its parent objects ([validated by: names the complete path of a nested missing required property](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L50)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46); [validated by: names a wrong-typed property and expected type without returning its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L76)).
+- A rejected call emits a warning that names the tool, failing property path and failed constraint without including the rejected property value ([validated by: logs a rejected field and constraint without logging its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L124)).
+- When `input` supplies a string outside a property's declared `enum`, the rejection names the property and its allowed choices without returning the offending value ([validated by: names an enum property and its allowed choices without returning its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L102)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: passes valid input with an undeclared property through unchanged exactly once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L36)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema`.
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: compiles the current schema from a function-valued definition before execution](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L146)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
